From 612a5d896f830a6556834877a1b130a38f2ef5f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:38:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(release): publish the browser (wasm32) build under
 /app/ on the Pages site

A `wasm` job in release.yml (ubuntu-24.04, contents: read) builds the
browser shell with web/build-app-wasm.sh --release on the run's tree,
checks the page folder and uploads it as the wasm-app artifact. The
`site` job waits for it with !cancelled() (the publish pattern), places
the folder at app/ in the Zola output and re-checks it there before
upload-pages-artifact. A failed wasm build leaves app/ as the site's own
"not part of this copy" page (site/content/app.md) and a warning naming
the missing browser build; docs and release go out anyway.

web/check-app-page.sh asserts index.html, wasi_shim.js, camcraft-ui.js
and a real wasm module are present, and refuses root-absolute or
protocol-relative URLs and SharedArrayBuffer (Pages has no COOP/COEP).
The front page and the guide's first-run page link the app with what
works and what does not yet. No new trigger.

Fixes #1103

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
